"cf43676d-e669-59cb-a36a-466aeb9d25ec" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276064 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276393 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276429 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277130 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277318 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186276064 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277800 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "2a54ad9f-1c7c-5c9d-b381-6d0caba02b7d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275951 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276026 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276293 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276470 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276949 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186276026 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277842 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "4646bb7e-6a09-5531-8391-f1f097bfe6dc" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278311 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277842 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278311 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160459" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278311 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278311 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278311 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e574537-84e0-52ce-b8da-3afe1320a385" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278311 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278317 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277800 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278317 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160469" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278317 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278317 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{2-x},\\, & x\\ge -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278317 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "21dab0f5-e122-5ef2-bac0-e65430de8846" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278317 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{2-x}$ on the interval $x\\ge -1,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=-k{e}^{2-x}\\,{|}_{-1}^{\\infty }=k{e}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\nk{e}^{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k={e}^{-3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352199 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352199 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352199 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "44034972-5d1f-5833-9415-2cd62da27891" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352242 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{3}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352242 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352242 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "48b14eee-c397-5b3a-bbde-437ae5b44dfc" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352363 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352363 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352363 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "598b16fd-1efc-50d1-a858-b6a88ba1c0c3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352871 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352871 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352871 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "95ecc404-9569-54c3-a1aa-0054028eafc3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352895 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352895 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186352895 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "9a1d2d32-6223-5ff2-b0e1-73f1f39e0d50" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186354046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186352199 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186354046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186352242 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186354046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186352363 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186354046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186352871 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186354046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref